//! expect-check-fail: 'PAR_LEVEL' is a name of the C header
//! expect-check-fail: which 'test/compile_errors/lib/contracts/parity.with' imports and this module does not (§16.2b.15)
//! expect-check-fail: = help: import the library's contract in this module (`use contracts.<name>`), or its header
// A C header's name is seen by a module that imports the header or the
// library's contract. This module imports `parity_user`, which does; that
// does not bring the header's names here, and the error says so and names
// the fix. It used to read "private to its package (declared in
// '…/contract.with')", which blamed the wrong file (#3521).
use parity_user

fn main:
    print(f"{level()} {PAR_LEVEL}")
